{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00138",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.0,
      "end_seconds": 4.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Doctor? Hi. I hope I've got the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.18,
      "end_seconds": 9.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.13,
      "end_seconds": 20.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.59,
      "text": "It's a bad cough, mostly. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.21,
      "end_seconds": 24.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.74,
      "end_seconds": 28.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "I mean, for ten days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.21,
      "end_seconds": 35.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Mm-hm. Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.54,
      "end_seconds": 55.6,
      "duration_seconds": 19.06,
      "text": "It happens a couple of times a week. A eight out of ten, I suppose. I took the morning off to come in today. And there's a tight chest as well, about two weeks now. Oh, about tight chest, I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.3,
      "end_seconds": 60.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Have you had any night sweats, coughing up blood or leg swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.56,
      "end_seconds": 64.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.59,
      "end_seconds": 67.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I see. Any chest pain or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.4,
      "end_seconds": 72.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "No chest pain or weight loss, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.86,
      "end_seconds": 75.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.93,
      "end_seconds": 82.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Yes, I had a bypass operation, six years ago. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.1,
      "end_seconds": 88.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Alright, what about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.46,
      "end_seconds": 92.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.33,
      "end_seconds": 94.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.34,
      "end_seconds": 96.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Yes, heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.69,
      "end_seconds": 100.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.94,
      "end_seconds": 103.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.07,
      "end_seconds": 106.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.8,
      "end_seconds": 116.5,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I'm on clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.94,
      "end_seconds": 117.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm-hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.96,
      "end_seconds": 124.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Paracetamol. I take it 500 milligrams, when needed. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.17,
      "end_seconds": 127.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.55,
      "end_seconds": 130.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.75,
      "end_seconds": 134.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.88,
      "end_seconds": 149.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.0,
      "end_seconds": 171.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 115 over 70, respiratory rate 16. And oxygen saturation is 96 percent, heart rate 102, temp 39.2 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.69,
      "end_seconds": 173.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.32,
      "end_seconds": 193.16,
      "duration_seconds": 18.84,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.41,
      "end_seconds": 196.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.01,
      "end_seconds": 202.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Okay, I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.3,
      "end_seconds": 206.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.19,
      "end_seconds": 228.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "There are a few scattered wheezes on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.61,
      "end_seconds": 231.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "I'll just listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.95,
      "end_seconds": 242.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "No crackles at the bases."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.59,
      "end_seconds": 265.97,
      "duration_seconds": 18.38,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with acute bronchitis. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a bad cough for ten days, and no leg swelling or coughing up blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.93,
      "end_seconds": 268.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.35,
      "end_seconds": 297.61,
      "duration_seconds": 28.26,
      "text": "We should do blood tests for cough. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Let's get a chest X-ray, for cough. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'd like you to take salbutamol inhaler, 100 micrograms, two puffs when needed, for one week. That should help with wheeze. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.28,
      "end_seconds": 324.11,
      "duration_seconds": 22.83,
      "text": "I'll start you on azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for three days. That's for chest infection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Steam and warm fluids can ease the cough, and try to sleep with your head propped up. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.53,
      "end_seconds": 331.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if you become breathless or cough up blood. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.1,
      "end_seconds": 334.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.6,
      "end_seconds": 345.92,
      "duration_seconds": 10.32,
      "text": "Please come and see me in a week. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.85,
      "end_seconds": 356.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "So, I take the salbutamol inhaler, 100 micrograms, two puffs when needed and take the azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.33,
      "end_seconds": 362.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.04,
      "end_seconds": 366.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, doctor, thanks."
    }
  ]
}